# Marathon — optional dev/QA WiFi pre-seed.
#
# Copy this file to scripts/qemu/wifi-preset.conf (gitignored), fill in
# real SSID and PSK, then re-build the image. setup-trees.sh detects
# the file and generates a NetworkManager keyfile into the duranium
# tree's mkosi.skeleton, so the device joins WiFi automatically on
# first boot — no need to walk through OOBE just to ssh in.
#
# Production builds should NOT have wifi-preset.conf present.
# .gitignore prevents accidental commit of secrets, but the responsibility
# for keeping it off shipping images stays with the operator.
#
# Format: plain shell key=value pairs. Quoted values OK; no `export`.
# SSID and PSK ONLY. WPA2-PSK is assumed (the common case for home
# networks). For enterprise auth, write the nmconnection by hand into
# scripts/qemu/duranium-overlay/mkosi.images/base/mkosi.skeleton/etc/
# NetworkManager/system-connections/marathon-dev.nmconnection at mode
# 0600 — setup-trees.sh leaves files there alone if no .conf is set.

SSID="YourNetworkName"
PSK="YourPassphrase"

# Optional. Defaults to "wlan0". Override if the device's interface
# name differs (some pmaports profiles bind to a specific wlan).
# INTERFACE_NAME="wlan0"
